This repository is not licensed as a whole. It holds several independently
licensed projects, each in its own top-level folder with its own LICENSE and
NOTICE file. Take the terms from the folder the code came from. Canonical copies
of the Apache-2.0 and GPL-3.0-only terms are also kept under LICENSES/ so the
standard grants are easy for people and release tooling to locate.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE PROJECTS

  Snowknife/               GPL-3.0-only    LICENSE.txt · NOTICE
      The extractor, bundle exporter and ISO packer, in Snowknife/, with its test
      suite alongside in Snowknife.Tests/. Both are covered by the same terms. The
      two nested entries below are carve-outs this row does not reach.

  Snowknife/SSX-Library/  upstream        LICENSE.txt
      A git submodule, originally by GlitcherOG. It sits inside Snowknife/ because
      that is the only project that builds against it, but it keeps its upstream
      terms; neither the row above nor anything else here relicenses it.

  Snowknife/Snowknife/schemas/
                          Apache-2.0      schemas/LICENSE
      The JSON interchange contracts, carved out under a permissive licence so
      that consumers outside the program can implement against them freely.
      Apache-2.0 is one-way compatible with GPLv3; Snowknife/NOTICE sets out what
      that means for a build of Snowknife itself.

  Slopesmith/             Apache-2.0      LICENSE · NOTICE
      The course-authoring editor and its API service. One scoped exception:
      tools/retopology/quadwild-patches/ holds modifications to third-party
      retopology programs and is conveyed under their upstream licences (GPL-3.0,
      MIT and BSD-style); see that folder's own README and LICENSE files.

  Unity/                   Apache-2.0      LICENSE · NOTICE
      The Unity editor importer and the VRChat and Basis runtimes.

  Trailmap/                Apache-2.0      LICENSE · NOTICE
      The interoperability specification and its research tooling.

Except for the canonical standard-license texts under LICENSES/, everything else
tracked in this repository is Apache-2.0. That is a rule, not an inventory: any
tracked path not inside one of the folders named above or LICENSES/ is covered by
it, whether or not it existed when this file was written. Examples include the
repository governance and build files, release history, tools/, Blender/, and
ResearchData/. The rule governs if these examples ever become stale.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT NONE OF THESE LICENSE

No retail game asset is included in this repository, and none is licensed by any
grant above. Disc-backed tools operate only on a user-supplied disc image. What
they produce from that image is derived from Electronic Arts' copyrighted work,
is generated on the user's own machine, and is excluded from version control.
The project grants no rights in retail-derived output. Users are responsible for
determining whether making or using an image and creating or using such output is
permitted under applicable law and contractual terms. Do not redistribute it
without authorization.

Current Slopesmith exports carry a machine-readable provenance classification.
`snowknife unity --public` is the guarded distribution path: it refuses retail-
derived and unclassified content and omits the disc-derived Shared asset pack.
That technical guard is conservative and is not itself a license or legal opinion.

SSX, SSX Tricky, SSX 3 and SSX On Tour are trademarks of Electronic Arts Inc.
This project is not endorsed by or affiliated with EA or its licensors, and is
not sponsored by them. Rights in the music and voice performances on a retail
disc are held by their publishers, labels and performers and are licensed to
Electronic Arts; no grant in this repository extends to them.

Each project's NOTICE carries the full scope, trademark and third-party
statements for its own material.
